meta {
  name: Analyze Chop Trap
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/llm/analyze/TSLA?timeframe=M5&session=RTH&fact=Supertrend flipped BULLISH 1 bar ago&fact=3 Supertrend flips in the last 5 bars (whipsaw)&fact=ADX 14 and falling&fact=Signal bar range is 3.2 ATR (climax bar)
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  timeframe: M5
  session: RTH
  fact: Supertrend flipped BULLISH 1 bar ago
  fact: 3 Supertrend flips in the last 5 bars (whipsaw)
  fact: ADX 14 and falling
  fact: Signal bar range is 3.2 ATR (climax bar)
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # LLM Analyze — Chop / Trap

  Same endpoint as "Analyze Clean Setup", but the briefing describes a messy,
  low-quality setup: a brand-new flip inside a whipsaw, a weak/falling ADX, and
  a climax (over-extended) signal bar.

  Expect the analyst to SKIP with a LOW conviction and to surface risk flags
  such as "recent whipsaw", "falling ADX", and "climax bar". Use this request as
  the counter-example when tuning the system prompt — a good configuration should
  clearly separate this from the clean setup.

  Edit the `fact` lines (and the ticker/timeframe/session) to probe other
  scenarios. Requires `app.llm.enabled=true` and a reachable local runtime.
}
